<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Free-field Born-term cross-check against the 2020 reference data at
  ~/lqcd/npr_momfrac/testing/free_field/born_term.h5

  Setup matches testing/free_field/zero_field_npr.qlua exactly:
    Lx = 16, Lt = 48, unit gauge field, mq = -0.2450 (kappa = 1/7.51),
    csw = 1.2493, bcs = {1, 1, 1, -1}, bvec = {0, 0, 0, 0.5}.

  clovCoeff is kept at 1.2493 rather than zeroed. With U = 1 the field
  strength vanishes, so the clover term must drop out on its own; leaving
  the coefficient in place tests that instead of assuming it.

  NORMALIZATION. born_term.h5 was made by compute_npr, which uses a
  MOMENTUM WALL source and projects through the sink, giving V * S~(p) and
  V * S~ V~_mu S~. This measurement uses a POINT source, giving S~(p) and
  S~ V~_mu S~. In the free field S(x,y) depends only on x - y, so the two
  differ by exactly V = 16^3 * 48 = 196608 in every entry, independent of
  the source point. That single global constant is itself a check.

  EXPECTED RESULT. The operator insertion is a pure point-split gamma_mu
  term with no Wilson piece, so S~(p) cancels under amputation and the
  tree-level vertex is independent of kappa, csw and the Wilson term:

      Gamma_mu(p) = -2i sin(p_mu) gamma_mu,   p_mu = 2 pi (k_mu + b_mu) / L_mu

  with the FULL angle sin(p_mu), not the half-angle 2 sin(p_mu / 2).

  The time direction carries a known boundary correction. Antiperiodicity is
  implemented by flipping U_3 on the last time slice inside the Dirac
  operator, while seqSource uses the RAW link, so one slice per term enters
  with the wrong sign. Each slice carries weight 1 / L_t, giving

      Gamma_3(p) = -2i sin(p_3) (1 - 2 / L_t) gamma_3

  i.e. 23/24 at L_t = 48. Verified to 1e-14 at all 1296 momenta of
  born_term.h5. This is a convention, not a bug: it cancels in Z provided
  the Born term is generated at the SAME L_t as the data.

  Momenta: born_term.h5 stores the full k in [0,5]^4 box (1296). This run
  takes the [0,2]^4 sub-box (81), all of which are present in the reference.
  Widen k_max to 5 5 5 5 for the complete comparison.
-->
<chroma>
<Param>
  <InlineMeasurements>
    <elem>
      <Name>NPR_MOMFRAC</Name>
      <Frequency>1</Frequency>
      <Param>
        <version>1</version>

        <!-- Free field is translation invariant, so the source point is
             arbitrary; the origin keeps the phases clean. -->
        <t_srce>0 0 0 0</t_srce>

        <mom_range>
          <k_min>0 0 0 0</k_min>
          <k_max>2 2 2 2</k_max>
        </mom_range>

        <!-- Must agree with the time component of FermionBC/boundary. -->
        <bvec>0 0 0 0.5</bvec>

        <output_type>TEXT</output_type>
        <output_file>./freefield_born.txt</output_file>

        <FermionAction>
          <FermAct>CLOVER</FermAct>
          <Mass>-0.2450</Mass>
          <clovCoeff>1.2493</clovCoeff>
          <AnisoParam>
            <anisoP>false</anisoP><t_dir>3</t_dir><xi_0>1</xi_0><nu>1</nu>
          </AnisoParam>
          <FermionBC>
            <FermBC>SIMPLE_FERMBC</FermBC>
            <boundary>1 1 1 -1</boundary>
          </FermionBC>
        </FermionAction>

        <InvertParam>
          <invType>CG_INVERTER</invType>
          <RsdCG>1.0e-14</RsdCG>
          <MaxCG>10000</MaxCG>
        </InvertParam>

      </Param>
      <NamedObject>
        <gauge_id>default_gauge_field</gauge_id>
      </NamedObject>
    </elem>

  </InlineMeasurements>
  <nrow>16 16 16 48</nrow>
</Param>

<RNG><Seed><elem>11</elem><elem>11</elem><elem>11</elem><elem>0</elem></Seed></RNG>
<Cfg>
  <cfg_type>UNIT</cfg_type>
  <cfg_file>dummy</cfg_file>
</Cfg>
</chroma>
